diff --git a/DOCS/man/options.rst b/DOCS/man/options.rst
index f0b9f7f..835d00d 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/options.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/options.rst
@@ -6174,6 +6174,33 @@ them.
     The slope of the sigmoid curve used for ``--sigmoid-upscaling``, must be a
     float between 1.0 and 20.0. Defaults to 6.5 if not specified.
 
+``--crt-beam=<yes|no>``
+    Enable the Blur Busters CRT Electron Beam Simulator on ``gpu-next``.
+    Default: no. Requires SDR, display-sync and interpolation disabled.
+    A native:simulated CRT refresh ratio of at least 2:1 is required.
+    The effect operates on each presented refresh, with three owned cycle
+    images and a clock independent of video PTS. Pause shows a complete image.
+    If supported presentation feedback reports skipped refreshes, the effect
+    stays inactive until a reset (seek, resume or toggling the option).
+
+``--crt-beam-scans=<1|2>``
+    Number of simulated CRT refreshes per video frame. Default: 2.
+    This repeats the original source image without motion interpolation.
+    For 25 fps use a 100 Hz display; for 24000/1001 fps prefer 120000/1001 Hz.
+    The original playback speed is preserved with ``video-sync=display-vdrop``.
+
+``--crt-beam-gain=<0..1>``
+    Linear-light brightness versus persistence tradeoff. Default: 0 (automatic
+    gain = simulated CRT Hz / native display Hz, as in TestUFO Auto Calc).
+    A positive value selects a fixed gain. Lower values reduce persistence
+    and brightness; 1 preserves average energy at the cost of bright-pixel
+    persistence. The output transfer must match the SDR display response.
+
+``--crt-beam-debug=<yes|no>``
+    Log each CRT render's presentation index, cycle, latched source ID, phase,
+    native:CRT ratio and gain. Default: no. This is a diagnostic trace of
+    rendering/submission, not proof of physical scan-out on a display.
+
 ``--interpolation``
     Reduce stuttering caused by mismatches in the video fps and display refresh
     rate (also known as judder).
